Sval: The address bar's open-tab rows come from Sval's tree

An inactive workspace's tabs are nodes of Sval's tree, not Firefox tabs, so
`UrlbarProviderPlaces`' open pages cannot see them, and Sval's provider lists
them (`SvalLauncherTabs`). Two changes no API offers:

- A switch-to-tab result's payload is validated against a closed schema, so
  the fields Sval's rows carry are added to it: the node, its workspace's
  name, colour, mark and emoji, whether that is an agent's, and whether it
  is the window's own.
- Firefox's own switch-to-tab row for a page the tree holds as a tab would
  list the tab a second time, and picking it would bypass the panel's
  workspace switch. The muxer drops it, asking Sval which pages those are.
  Sval's rows are one per node, so they are not deduplicated by address: a
  page open in two workspaces is two rows.

diff --git a/browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarMuxerStandard.sys.mjs b/browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarMuxerStandard.sys.mjs
index 624cb2adcc..9d93c76328 100644
--- a/browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarMuxerStandard.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarMuxerStandard.sys.mjs
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@ const lazy = {};
 ChromeUtils.defineESModuleGetters(lazy, {
   QuickSuggest: "moz-src:///browser/components/urlbar/QuickSuggest.sys.mjs",
   SearchService: "moz-src:///toolkit/components/search/SearchService.sys.mjs",
+  SvalLauncherTabs:
+    "moz-src:///browser/components/sval/SvalLauncherTabs.sys.mjs",
   UrlbarPrefs: "moz-src:///browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarPrefs.sys.mjs",
   UrlbarProviderOpenTabs:
     "moz-src:///browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderOpenTabs.sys.mjs",
@@ -1021,9 +1023,16 @@ class MuxerUnifiedComplete extends UrlbarMuxer {
       }
     }
 
+    // Sval lists the tabs of its tree itself, one row for each, so one page
+    // open in two workspaces is two rows.
+    if (lazy.SvalLauncherTabs.replaces(result, state.context)) {
+      return false;
+    }
+
     // Discard switch-to-tab results that dupes another switch-to-tab result.
     if (
       result.type == UrlbarUtils.RESULT_TYPE.TAB_SWITCH &&
+      !result.payload.svalNodeId &&
       state.addedSwitchTabUrls.has(makeMapKeyForTabResult(result))
     ) {
       return false;
